Newspeak3
'Test'
(* newspeak-spec.pdf 3.6: "It is a compile-time error to define a method or
   closure that has a parameter and a local with the same name." An
   activation's parameter slots and local slots are one set of slots -- 3.6
   gives it "zero or more parameter slots, one for each formal parameter"
   and "zero or more local slots, one for each slot declaration in the body"
   -- so shadow: defines value twice, and the program is not to be
   compiled at all.

   The resolver has no such check: it gives the local its own register, the
   method runs and answers 5 at exit status 0, so which of the two `value`
   means is decided silently.

   The check does not exist, so neither does its wording. The recorded
   stderr is the resolver's existing duplicate-definition message
   (crates/ns-runtime/src/resolver/mod.rs, "class `{name}` has multiple
   definitions of `{duplicate}`", printed as `resolve error: ...` at exit
   status 1 by crates/ns-cli/src/source.rs) with the construct named as the
   method rather than the class. It is a proposal, not a derivation: what
   3.6 fixes is that the program is refused before it runs, and whoever
   implements the check settles the text. Skipped until it exists. *)
class Spec36ParameterAndLocalClash usingPlatform: p = Object new (| t = p transcript. |) (
    shadow: value = ( | value | value:: 5. ^value )
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        t show: (self shadow: 1) printString; newLine.
    )
) : ()
